# Testing (next-dato)

Runner: **Vitest** (`npm test`, `npm run test:watch`).

## What to test

- `resolve*Options()` — defaults, `advanced_options`, PT labels, snake_case aliases
- `resolve*Image()`, `link-block`, `dast-plain-text`, JSON-LD builders
- `compare-secret`, validation use-cases in `core/`
- Pure functions in `lib/` with branching logic

## What to skip unless asked

- Snapshot tests of full components
- Testing that React renders without asserting behavior
- Mocking DatoCMS for every page test

## Conventions

- File: `{module}.test.ts` beside `{module}.ts`
- Use descriptive `it("...")` strings — behavior, not implementation
- Cover both camelCase and snake_case when reading CMS records
- No secrets or real tokens in fixtures

## CI

- Unit: [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../.github/workflows/ci.yml) — typecheck, lint, test, security:audit, build, codegen:check
- E2E smoke: [`.github/workflows/e2e.yml`](../../.github/workflows/e2e.yml) — `npm run test:e2e` (Playwright)

## Before merge

```bash
npm run typecheck && npm test
```

See [docs/QUALITY-GATES.md](../../docs/QUALITY-GATES.md) pillar 7.
